1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,430
This is LayerCue.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:07,320
It sends a presentation to a screen, in layers.

3
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:10,290
It runs on Mac and Windows.

4
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:13,100
A video runs underneath.

5
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:15,290
Words sit on top.

6
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:18,000
A logo stays in a corner.

7
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:21,410
Each one comes and goes on its own.

8
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:27,500
By the end you will point at every part of this window.

9
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:29,740
Today we only look.

10
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:33,010
You send nothing to the stage today.

11
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:38,170
The window has four areas.

12
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:40,620
The sidebar on the left.

13
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:43,000
The slides in the middle.

14
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,580
The band across the top.

15
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:48,620
The status bar along the bottom.

16
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:50,990
Pick on the left.

17
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:52,780
Click in the middle.

18
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:54,390
Watch the top.

19
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:56,580
Adjust on the right.

20
00:00:57,230 --> 00:01:00,920
The right means Slide settings, at the band's end.

21
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:04,210
Every later episode hangs on it.

22
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:08,850
I start on the left.

23
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,260
Cue Sheets sit on top.

24
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:15,160
A cue sheet is the running order for one event.

25
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:18,730
Tour lines up six short guides, in order.

26
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:23,010
The Library drawer is below, under a line.

27
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:26,840
A library is a folder of presentations.

28
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:30,310
A presentation is one set of slides.

29
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:33,600
The number at right is the slide count.

30
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:36,750
I press the double arrow.

31
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:40,370
I press it again to lower it.

32
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:43,300
Pointing at it does not raise it.

33
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:49,440
I click Start here, inside the Tour cue sheet.

34
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:53,580
The middle shows every presentation in it, in order.

35
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:58,710
Each has a title bar with its name and slide count.

36
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:01,430
Five buttons sit at its right.

37
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,920
Add File.

38
00:02:02,970 --> 00:02:04,040
Link.

39
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:05,150
Edit.

40
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,060
Layer for this list.

41
00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:09,230
Presentation settings.

42
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:12,260
Under the bar are the slide cards.

43
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:15,780
Under the picture, a Text badge and the name.

44
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:18,940
A click on a card's picture sends it out.

45
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:22,200
No confirmation, no second step.

46
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:25,800
I do not click a picture today.

47
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:28,340
That is Episode 3.

48
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:33,750
Now the top band, where you watch.

49
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,800
The tile at the left is Screen 1.

50
00:02:36,850 --> 00:02:40,780
Here it is a virtual screen, no projector needed.

51
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:45,540
The power switch at the right end turns the output on and off.

52
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:51,430
Under the preview, Layers shown picks which layers this monitor shows.

53
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:55,510
Beside the preview, the layer column shows what is up.

54
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:58,470
CLEAR on top, then seven layers.

55
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,350
Five overlays.

56
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,320
F for foreground.

57
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:04,310
B for background.

58
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:07,340
Next, the sound meter.

59
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:10,290
Then Music, on its own channel.

60
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:13,210
At the right end, Slide settings.

61
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:17,210
Option + slide to load means look, not send.

62
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:22,900
The status bar reads left to right.

63
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:24,690
Show and Edit.

64
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:28,510
The On air chip counts the monitors that are showing.

65
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:31,860
The speaker box is your sound device.

66
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:35,510
The dot and title say what is on stage.

67
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:39,120
Tell us what's wrong sends us a note.

68
00:03:39,170 --> 00:03:41,470
The slider sets card size.

69
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:44,400
The pencil is Lock editing.

70
00:03:44,450 --> 00:03:46,690
The gear is Settings.

71
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:52,930
This demo is scripted, on a virtual screen.

72
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:55,080
The event is made up.

73
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:58,020
A video goes to the background.

74
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:00,610
The B cell turns amber.

75
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:04,430
Words go to the foreground, on top.

76
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:06,520
F turns indigo.

77
00:04:06,570 --> 00:04:09,530
A logo goes to overlay one.

78
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:12,030
Cell 1 turns green.

79
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,650
I change the words.

80
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:17,040
The video never stops.

81
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:21,040
The x beside F takes only the words down.

82
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:24,600
That is the whole point of layers.

83
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:29,970
I click Edit in the status bar.

84
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:34,390
The whole window becomes the slide editor.

85
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,760
The slides stand in a strip down the left.

86
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:40,150
I click Show to come back.

87
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:43,600
That is the main window.

88
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:49,610
You can now point at every part of the window.

89
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:55,270
Next: Episode 2 — Install, First Launch and Settings.

